 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? That's common with cheap bearings. You can usually fix it by cleaning and greasing them. Do you want try that, or would you rather just buy replacements? Sorry, but that's bit of a last resort. Cooking oil wears fast and can make the chain dirtier. A proper grease lasts much longer. Pop open a new tube of grip tape, or do you want to try cleaning and greasing first? Clean it, then blow it dry before applying grease. Not really. A thin coat of greasing protects the bearings without making them oily. Which would you rather do, greasing or tapeing?",
